{
  "_comment": [
    "The shared parity fixture: the contract between the Rust crate config-layers and its TypeScript twin @osdlc/config-layers.",
    "Both suites read this file (Rust: tests/parity.rs; TypeScript: packages/ts/config-layers/tests/parity.test.ts) and assert the same results.",
    "A case added on either side goes here, never in one twin's own suite.",
    "Only behaviour both twins share is listed. The README's differences table lists what is left out, for example empty YAML documents and integers beyond 2^53.",
    "A case with `missing: true` passes no value at all (Rust None, TypeScript undefined). An `error: true` case checks that the read fails, not the message text.",
    "The path cases use POSIX paths. The Rust suite runs them on Unix only."
  ],
